Attribution

Source dataset: ogbn-arxiv, part of the Open Graph Benchmark (OGB)
  https://ogb.stanford.edu/docs/nodeprop/#ogbn-arxiv

Cite as:

  Weihua Hu, Matthias Fey, Marinka Zitnik, Yuxiao Dong, Hongyu Ren,
  Bowen Liu, Michele Catasta, and Jure Leskovec. "Open Graph Benchmark:
  Datasets for Machine Learning on Graphs." NeurIPS 2020.

ogbn-arxiv is itself built on the Microsoft Academic Graph (MAG); OGB's own
attribution for this dataset additionally cites:

  Kuansan Wang, Zhihong Shen, Chiyuan Huang, Chieh-Han Wu, Yuxiao Dong, and
  Anshul Kanakia. "Microsoft Academic Graph: When experts are not enough."
  Quantitative Science Studies, 1(1):396-413, 2020.

The node feature embeddings OGB derives from titles/abstracts use the
skip-gram model of:

  Tomas Mikolov, Ilya Sutskever, Kai Chen, Greg S. Corrado, and Jeff Dean.
  "Distributed Representations of Words and Phrases and their
  Compositionality." NeurIPS 2013.

(This fixture does not use OGB's precomputed feature embeddings — it mines
its own supervised pairs from the raw title/abstract text — but the citation
is reproduced here because it is part of OGB's own required attribution for
ogbn-arxiv, per the references above.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes made to the original data

This fixture is a derived, DOWNSAMPLED excerpt, not the full dataset:

* Restricted to a committed 4000-paper subset of ogbn-arxiv (see
  `arxiv_subset_ids.txt`, a vendored copy of the subset id list; the subset
  is otherwise unmodified from the OGB release).
* Same-subject (anchor, positive, negative) supervised pairs mined
  deterministically from that subset (seeded, sorted-id traversal; see
  `manifest.json.split_rule` and `README.md`).
  Title+abstract text is clipped to 1500 characters per field.
  1500 pairs total mined; only the 128 held-out pairs' full text is
  redistributed here (`heldout_pairs.jsonl`) — the 1372 train-side pairs are
  represented as ids + a SHA-256 digest of their text, not the text itself
  (`train_ids_sha256.json`).

